          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "qollâb bâfi is built in Persian on qollâb, 'hook', a loan usually traced to Arabic, and bâf, the stem of native bâftan, 'to knit, to weave'. EtymDB has no entry for it."
